;;; A written fact's `:using` that names a fact no state holds loads, and the refutation that rests
;;; on the fact reports the empty core —
;;; M1f **W87**, register row `W87/written-using-never-held`, filed by S1f.7.9 (T1f.7.9.2,
;;; 2026-11-11).
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; One guest, the fact `(paid Ann :rule seat :using ((invited Zoe)))`, and the rules `seat` and
;;; `clash`. Nothing states or derives `(invited Zoe)`, and `Zoe` is named nowhere else. Root is
;;; dead. No candidate.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; Not ruled: it is F24's question. Under (a) and (b) the program is refused at load: under
;;; (b), `:using` names facts the program holds. Under (c) it loads as written, marked as not
;;; checked, and the written fact is a given in every core, so the core is `(paid Ann)`.
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; At `91b12be8`, release: the program loads; R is empty, root dead, `unsat core ∅, the empty
;;; set: the refutation rests on no fact`, `refuted by clash`. `ein saturate --dump` prints
;;; `(paid Ann :rule seat)`: the `:using` is not printed.
;;; Open, and F24's: what a written provenance may claim is the user's question, not ruled.

(relation paid Guest :why "{?1} has paid")
(relation seated Guest :why "{?1} is seated")
(is-a Ann Guest)
(paid Ann :rule seat :using ((invited Zoe)))
(rule seat () :match (paid ?g) :assert (seated ?g) :why "{?g} is seated: they have paid")
(rule clash () :match (and (seated ?g) (paid ?g)) :assert (false) :why "{?g} is seated and has paid, which this party forbids")
(solve :hypothesis-relations ())
